1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:02,113
If Earth were this marble,

2
00:00:02,113 --> 00:00:03,750
how big is the universe?

3
00:00:04,650 --> 00:00:07,339
The Sun would be a ball over 1 metre wide.

4
00:00:07,339 --> 00:00:10,150
More than 1 million Earths could fit inside.

5
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:14,347
And that ball would sit 117 metres away.

6
00:00:14,347 --> 00:00:16,780
Longer than a football field.

7
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,566
Neptune, the last planet,

8
00:00:19,566 --> 00:00:21,940
would circle 3.5 kilometres out.

9
00:00:22,840 --> 00:00:24,429
Now shrink all of that.

10
00:00:24,429 --> 00:00:27,290
Put every planet's orbit in one coffee cup.

11
00:00:28,190 --> 00:00:31,144
Earth is now barely 1 millimetre from the Sun.

12
00:00:31,144 --> 00:00:32,190
And our galaxy?

13
00:00:33,090 --> 00:00:35,815
As big as your city? All of Canada?

14
00:00:35,815 --> 00:00:37,140
Still too small.

15
00:00:38,040 --> 00:00:40,668
The Milky Way would cover North America,

16
00:00:40,668 --> 00:00:42,420
from the Arctic to Panama.

17
00:00:44,840 --> 00:00:45,710
Shrink again,

18
00:00:45,710 --> 00:00:48,380
until the whole Milky Way is a dinner plate.

19
00:00:49,280 --> 00:00:51,569
Andromeda, our largest neighbour,

20
00:00:51,569 --> 00:00:54,250
is a bigger plate, about 6 metres away.

21
00:00:56,080 --> 00:00:58,578
And the universe we can see?

22
00:00:58,578 --> 00:01:00,409
230 kilometres wide.

23
00:01:00,409 --> 00:01:03,406
As far as Montreal to Quebec City,

24
00:01:03,406 --> 00:01:06,320
with galaxies in every direction.

25
00:01:07,220 --> 00:01:09,610
And on one plate, inside one cup,

26
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:12,410
is a single blue marble. So, once more.
